# Logs: one JSONL per day plus the watcher log, all named by date, all pruned by
# logRetentionDays. Nothing here is worth keeping and a year of it names every
# file you have ever moved.
logs/*

# Working copies, .bak snapshots and scratch diagnostics. Nothing here is part of
# the tool - it is what you keep while changing something and delete when it is
# done. Ignored so none of it can reach a published repo.
backup/*

# Your policy, not the project's. It names your drive letters, your library paths
# and your account, so it stays on this machine. Copy config.example.json to
# config.json and edit that instead - the scripts look for config.json and fall
# back to the example if it is missing.
config.json

# Balancer runtime state, and the disk-identity map the failing-drive gate writes.
# Both are per-machine: state holds a pid and a phase, and diskmap records which
# physical disk held each failing disk number.
#
# logs/givenback.json used to be here, for the give-back ledger. The give-back is
# gone - nothing moves backwards - so nothing writes that file any more.
logs/state.json

# Nothing should land here, but a killed copy can leave a .tmp next to a ledger
# that a crash prevented from being renamed into place.
*.tmp

# Editor state. Created by whatever editor you opened the folder in, and specific
# to this machine - it records which commands you have approved. Nobody else wants
# it, and 'git add -A' would otherwise pick it up on its own.
.vscode/